IMPORT prelude

-- Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970 (Singapore) -- how profit meets a reserve deficit (s 6(4)), the board's size,
-- terms, disqualification, quorum and conflicts (ss 7, 8, 10, 12, 13), the secrecy and information offences that bind MAS
-- staff and contractors (ss 14A, 14B, 14C), immunity and indemnity (ss 22, 22A), primary dealers for MAS securities (ss 145,
-- 146, 148, 149, 150), and prosecution and composition (ss 173, 176).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MASA1970.txt, with
-- amendments to Act 12 of 2024 (in force 30 August 2024) shown. Parts 4A, 4B and 5C and ss 31 to 126, 152 to 163 and 177
-- are shown as repealed by Act 18 of 2022.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 30 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. It is an institutional Act: most of it
-- sets up the Authority and lists its powers. SCOPED to the rules with decision content. Not encoded: the objects and
-- functions (s 4), the list of banking powers (s 23), investment of funds, the Government banker role, special loans (s 26),
-- the real-time gross settlement system (s 29A), the Financial Sector Development Fund (Part 5), book-entry MAS securities
-- (Part 5A), accounts and audit, and the Schedule of written laws.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970`

§§ `6(4) -- net profit and a reserve deficit`

-- s 6(3): of each year's net profit, "such part ... as the Authority may determine must be paid to the Government and the
-- remainder ... credited to the General Reserve Fund" -- "Subject to subsection (4)".
-- s 6(4): where the Fund is in deficit at year end, (a) if net profit is LARGER than the deficit, "an amount of not less than
-- the net profit necessary to offset the deficit" must be credited; (b) if net profit is SMALLER THAN OR EQUAL TO the deficit,
-- "the whole of the net profit must be credited".
--
-- Without a deficit the Act fixes no minimum credit: the Authority decides the split. A loss year credits nothing (inference:
-- the Act speaks only of crediting net profit).
GIVEN `net profit` IS A NUMBER, `deficit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the least amount that must go to the General Reserve Fund` MEANS
    IF `net profit` AT MOST 0 OR `deficit` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `net profit` GREATER THAN `deficit` THEN `deficit` ELSE `net profit`

GIVEN `net profit` IS A NUMBER, `deficit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be paid to the Government out of the year's profit` MEANS
    IF `net profit` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `net profit` MINUS `the least amount that must go to the General Reserve Fund` `net profit` `deficit`

§§ `7, 8 -- the board`

-- s 7(3): a chairperson appointed by the President on the Cabinet's recommendation and "(b) not less than 4 and not more than
-- 13 other directors". s 8(2)(b): directors "hold office for a term not exceeding 3 years and are eligible for re-appointment";
-- s 8(3): that does not apply to a director appointed managing director.
GIVEN `other directors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board is lawfully composed` IF
    `other directors` AT LEAST 4 AND `other directors` AT MOST 13

GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER, `is the managing director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the term of appointment is within the limit` IF
    `is the managing director` OR `term in years` AT MOST 3

§§ `10 -- disqualification and removal of directors`

-- s 10(1): "No person may be appointed as or remain a director of the Authority who is a director or salaried official of any
-- financial institution licensed or approved by the Authority under any written law."
-- s 10(2): the President MAY terminate a s 8(1) director who (a) resigns; (b) has a mental disorder and becomes incapable of
-- managing his or her affairs; (c) becomes bankrupt or compounds with creditors; (d) is convicted of an offence involving
-- dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude; (e) is guilty of serious misconduct in his or her duties; (f) "is absent, without leave,
-- from 3 consecutive meetings of the board"; or (g) fails to comply with s 13.
--
-- s 10(1) is a bar, not a discretion. s 10(2) is a discretion; none of its grounds removes a director automatically.
DECLARE Director HAS
    `is a director or salaried official of a licensed or approved financial institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a mental disorder and cannot manage own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is bankrupt or has compounded with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude` IS A BOOLEAN
    `guilty of serious misconduct in duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consecutive board meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER
    `failed to disclose an interest under section 13` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the director` IS A Director
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may not be or remain a director` IF
    `the director`'s `is a director or salaried official of a licensed or approved financial institution`

GIVEN `the director` IS A Director
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the President may terminate the appointment` IF
        `the director`'s `has resigned`
    OR  `the director`'s `has a mental disorder and cannot manage own affairs`
    OR  `the director`'s `is bankrupt or has compounded with creditors`
    OR  `the director`'s `convicted of an offence of dishonesty, fraud or moral turpitude`
    OR  `the director`'s `guilty of serious misconduct in duties`
    OR  `the director`'s `consecutive board meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `the director`'s `failed to disclose an interest under section 13`

§§ `12, 13 -- quorum, voting and interested directors`

-- s 12(2): "a quorum consists of 4 directors or a simple majority of the directors, whichever is the larger, and decisions are
-- to be adopted by a simple majority of the votes of the directors present and voting except that in the case of an equality
-- of votes the chairperson has a casting vote".
-- s 13(1), (2): a director interested in a contract must disclose it; afterwards the director "(a) must not take part in any
-- deliberation or decision of the board with respect to that contract; and (b) must be disregarded for the purpose of
-- constituting a quorum". s 13(3): no act of the board "may be questioned on the ground that a director has contravened this
-- section".
--
-- "A simple majority of the directors" is read as more than half of the directors in office (an inference: the Act does not
-- say whether the chairperson is counted; the cases count every director, chair included).
GIVEN `directors in office` IS A NUMBER, `counted as present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present` IF
    `counted as present` AT LEAST 4 AND `counted as present` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `directors in office`

GIVEN `directors in office` IS A NUMBER, `present` IS A NUMBER, `interested directors present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quorum is present for a contract in which directors are interested` IF
    `a quorum is present` `directors in office` (`present` MINUS `interested directors present`)

GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the chairperson's casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board decides in favour` IF
        `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
    OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the chairperson's casting vote is for`)

§§ `14A -- secrecy`

-- s 14A(1): a current or former director, officer or employee of the Authority "must not disclose to any person ANY
-- information" acquired in the performance of duties. (2): a current or former contractor, consultant or agent of the
-- Authority, or an employee of one, must not disclose "any information (OTHER THAN PERSONAL DATA about an individual)" so
-- acquired. (3): neither applies to disclosure (a) to perform duties; (b) as authorised by the Authority; (c) as permitted or
-- required by written law; (d) under a court order; (e) in prescribed circumstances. (5): $20,000 or 2 years or both.
--
-- A contractor disclosing personal data is outside s 14A(2) altogether (inference: other law, such as the Personal Data
-- Protection Act 2012 named in s 14, would have to reach it; s 14A(4) preserves such other law).
DECLARE Insider IS ONE OF
    `a director, officer or employee of the Authority`
    `a contractor, consultant or agent of the Authority, or its employee`
    `anyone else`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Insider, `acquired in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN, `is personal data` IS A BOOLEAN, `a subsection (3) exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence under section 14A` IF
        `acquired in performing duties`
    AND (NOT `a subsection (3) exception applies`)
    AND CONSIDER `who`
        WHEN `a director, officer or employee of the Authority` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a contractor, consultant or agent of the Authority, or its employee` THEN NOT `is personal data`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14B -- improper use of information`

-- s 14B(1) (MAS insiders) and (2) (contractors, consultants, agents and their employees; information "other than personal data
-- about an individual"): an offence if a person uses information in the Authority's possession acquired in performing duties,
-- the use "is not authorised by the Authority", the person knows or is "reckless as to whether the use is or is not
-- authorised", and AS A RESULT "(i) obtains a gain for the [person] or another person; (ii) causes harm to another individual;
-- or (iii) causes a loss to another person". $20,000 or 2 years or both.
-- (3): defence, proved "on a balance of probabilities", that (a) the information was "generally available information" at the
-- time, or (b) the use was permitted by law, under a court order, or in prescribed circumstances.
--
-- Unauthorised use without any gain, harm or loss is no offence under s 14B.
DECLARE `Use of information` HAS
    `user` IS AN Insider
    `acquired in performing duties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or was reckless that it was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gain, harm or loss resulted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved the information was generally available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved the use was permitted by law, court order or prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the use` IS A `Use of information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the user is within section 14B` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`'s `user`
    WHEN `a director, officer or employee of the Authority` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a contractor, consultant or agent of the Authority, or its employee` THEN NOT `the use`'s `is personal data`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the use` IS A `Use of information`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use is an offence under section 14B` IF
        `the user is within section 14B` `the use`
    AND `the use`'s `acquired in performing duties`
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `authorised by the Authority`)
    AND `the use`'s `knew or was reckless that it was unauthorised`
    AND `the use`'s `gain, harm or loss resulted`
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `proved the information was generally available`)
    AND (NOT `the use`'s `proved the use was permitted by law, court order or prescribed circumstances`)

§§ `14C -- re-identifying anonymised information`

-- s 14C(1): an offence if a current or former director, officer or employee of the Authority takes action to re-identify a
-- person to whom anonymised information held by the Authority relates, without the Authority's authority, knowing or reckless
-- as to that. $20,000 or 2 years or both. No gain, harm or loss is needed.
-- (2): defence that (a) the identity "is publicly available"; (b) the action is permitted by law, a court order or prescribed
-- circumstances; or (c) the defendant "(i) reasonably believed that the re-identification was for a specified purpose; and
-- (ii) notified the Authority ... as soon as was practicable" (specified purpose: Eleventh Schedule to the PDPA 2012).
--
-- s 14C reaches only MAS's own directors, officers and employees. A contractor who re-identifies commits no s 14C offence.
DECLARE `Re-identification` HAS
    `actor` IS AN Insider
    `authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or was reckless that it was unauthorised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved the identity was publicly available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved it was permitted by law, court order or prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably believed it was for a specified purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
    `notified the Authority as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Re-identification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 14C defence is made out` IF
        `the act`'s `proved the identity was publicly available`
    OR  `the act`'s `proved it was permitted by law, court order or prescribed circumstances`
    OR  (`the act`'s `reasonably believed it was for a specified purpose` AND `the act`'s `notified the Authority as soon as practicable`)

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Re-identification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the re-identification is an offence under section 14C` IF
        `the act`'s `actor` EQUALS `a director, officer or employee of the Authority`
    AND (NOT `the act`'s `authorised by the Authority`)
    AND `the act`'s `knew or was reckless that it was unauthorised`
    AND (NOT `a section 14C defence is made out` `the act`)

§§ `22, 22A -- immunity and indemnity`

-- s 22: no proceedings lie against (a) the Authority; (b) any director, officer or employee; (c) any public officer; (d) any
-- person on secondment or attachment to the Authority; or (e) any person appointed, approved or directed by the Minister or
-- the Authority to exercise its powers or assist it, "for anything done (including any statement made) or omitted to be done
-- in good faith" in the course of exercising powers, performing functions, or complying with the Act or any other written law.
-- s 22A(1), (2): the Authority MUST indemnify a person within s 22(b), (d) or (e) against costs reasonably incurred in
-- proceedings arising from such a good-faith act. Not (a) the Authority itself, and not (c) a public officer.
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the Authority`
    `a director, officer or employee`
    `a public officer`
    `a secondee to the Authority`
    `a person appointed or directed to exercise or assist the Authority's powers`
    `a regulated financial institution`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is a section 22 person` IF
    CONSIDER `the defendant`
    WHEN `a regulated financial institution` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of a power, function or compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no proceedings lie` IF
    `the defendant is a section 22 person` `the defendant` AND `acted in good faith` AND `in the course of a power, function or compliance`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of a power, function or compliance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority must indemnify the costs` IF
        `acted in good faith`
    AND `in the course of a power, function or compliance`
    AND CONSIDER `the defendant`
        WHEN `a director, officer or employee` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a secondee to the Authority` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a person appointed or directed to exercise or assist the Authority's powers` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `145, 146 -- primary dealers`

-- s 145(7): a person who is not a primary dealer and "carries on, or holds himself, herself or itself out as carrying on or
-- willing to carry on", the business of applying for MAS securities, or offering to redeem them, on behalf of another, is
-- guilty of an offence.
-- s 146(4): before modifying a dealer's conditions the Authority must, "unless ... it considers that it is not practicable or
-- desirable to do so", give notice allowing a time for representations "being at least 28 days after the date of service".
GIVEN `is an appointed primary dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `carries on or holds out the business for others` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the section 145(7) offence` IF
    (NOT `is an appointed primary dealer`) AND `carries on or holds out the business for others`

GIVEN `days allowed for representations` IS A NUMBER, `the Authority considers notice impracticable or undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the modification notice is adequate` IF
    `the Authority considers notice impracticable or undesirable` OR `days allowed for representations` AT LEAST 28

§§ `148, 149 -- orders against primary dealers and appeals`

-- s 148(2)(a): instead of cancelling, the Authority may "suspend the appointment for such period (not exceeding 6 months)".
-- s 148(7): an order under (1), (2) or (3) "does not take effect until the expiration of 21 days after the Authority has served
-- the notice of the order"; (9): a reprimand "takes effect on the date it is served".
-- s 149(1): a dealer may appeal to the Minister "within 14 days after the receipt" of an order under s 148(1), (2) or (3),
-- "except an order of reprimand"; the Minister's decision is final. (2)(a): an appealed cancellation "does not take effect
-- unless the order is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is ... dismissed ... or withdrawn"; (b) every other order
-- appealed against "takes effect and must be complied with until the determination of the appeal".
--
-- Read here: "until the expiration of 21 days" means effect from day 22 after service (inference). Whether s 149(2)(b) brings an
-- appealed suspension or penalty into effect before day 22 is not resolved by the text; the encoding keeps the 21 days.
DECLARE Order IS ONE OF
    `cancellation`
    `suspension`
    `reprimand`
    `a daily financial penalty`

GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension period is lawful` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `days since receipt` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order may be appealed to the Minister` IF
        `days since receipt` AT MOST 14
    AND CONSIDER `the order`
        WHEN `reprimand` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the order` IS AN Order, `days since service` IS A NUMBER, `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order has taken effect` IF
    CONSIDER `the order`
    WHEN `reprimand` THEN `days since service` AT LEAST 0
    WHEN `cancellation` THEN `days since service` GREATER THAN 21 AND (NOT `an appeal is pending`)
    OTHERWISE `days since service` GREATER THAN 21

§§ `Penalties, prosecution and composition -- ss 14A to 14C, 145, 150, 173, 175, 176`

-- s 14A(5), 14B(1), (2), 14C(1): fine up to $20,000, imprisonment up to 2 years, or both.
-- s 145(7): (a) an individual -- $125,000 or 3 years or both, and $12,500 a day for a continuing offence after conviction; (b)
-- any other case -- $250,000, and $25,000 a day.
-- s 150(6): failing without reasonable excuse to produce books or explain them on an inspection -- $50,000 or 2 years or both,
-- and $5,000 a day.
-- s 173: "No prosecution ... may be instituted without the consent in writing of the Public Prosecutor."
-- s 175: a District Court may try all offences under the Act "and impose the full penalty".
-- s 176(1): the Authority may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum of money not
-- exceeding one half of the amount of the maximum fine"; (1A) also one that was compoundable when committed but has ceased to
-- be. (2): on payment, "no further proceedings".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unauthorised disclosure, s 14A`
    `improper use of information, s 14B`
    `re-identification, s 14C`
    `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by an individual, s 145(7)(a)`
    `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by a company, s 145(7)(b)`
    `obstructing an inspection of a primary dealer, s 150(6)`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by an individual, s 145(7)(a)` THEN 125000
    WHEN `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by a company, s 145(7)(b)` THEN 250000
    WHEN `obstructing an inspection of a primary dealer, s 150(6)` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by an individual, s 145(7)(a)` THEN 36
    WHEN `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by a company, s 145(7)(b)` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 24

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by an individual, s 145(7)(a)` THEN 12500
    WHEN `acting as a primary dealer unappointed, by a company, s 145(7)(b)` THEN 25000
    WHEN `obstructing an inspection of a primary dealer, s 150(6)` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS (`the daily fine for a continuing offence` `the offence` TIMES `days continued after conviction`)

GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented in writing`

GIVEN `prescribed as compoundable now` IS A BOOLEAN, `was compoundable when committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may compound the offence` IF
    `prescribed as compoundable now` OR `was compoundable when committed`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Authority may collect to compound` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
